t_message="rockchip: rk3399: add routines to set vop clocks  Let vop aclk sources from CPLL, and vop dclk from NPLL.  The dclk freq is decided by the edid mode pixel_clock which may require high accuracy like 252750KHz. The pll_para_config() can calculate the dividers for PLL to output desired clock.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:51537 TEST=check display with the other patches  Change-Id: Icef58f87041905961772b69c6b8170d5a866a531 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342335 Tested-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="342335" owner_email="zhengsq@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/35/342335/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I629599f9e30d863cabf764e1372c38f0f39d5480" commit="ef5b0d7c7e6ef6d59f557132e5cf1af13d74d496" commit_message="rockchip: revert the common tsadc header  The tsadc of rk3288 and rk3399 are similar but not enough to share the same common driver, and we also decide to add a polarity setting for mainboards on rk3399 tsadc header. So we'd better split the tsadc header for each SoC.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:51537 TEST=build veyron_jerry  Change-Id: I629599f9e30d863cabf764e1372c38f0f39d5480 Signed-off-by: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342796 Tested-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="342796" owner_email="zhengsq@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/96/342796/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="Iffe54d3b09080d0f1ff31e8b3020d69510f07c95" commit="16afc36881b5cbe779eef1fefa78048578dac79d" commit_message="rockchip: rk3399: add tsadc driver  This patch configures clock for tsadc and then makes it in automatic mode to generate TSHUT when CPU temperature is higer than 120 degree Celsius.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52382,chrome-os-partner:51537 TEST=Set a lower tshut threshold(45C), run coreboot and check      that coreboot reboot again and again.  Change-Id: Iffe54d3b09080d0f1ff31e8b3020d69510f07c95 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Shunqian Zheng &lt;zhengsq@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342797 Tested-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shelley Chen &lt;shchen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="342797" owner_email="zhengsq@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/97/342797/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id808d4fe69eabed52a5c42c4a6d8e1098965c5cb" commit="8c69154cb69871969d532ce10b2c9468bd6586f0" commit_message="alsa_api_test: Add a test binary for ALSA API  Test snd_pcm_drop and snd_pcm_forward behavior. These two calls are needed for new CRAS scheduling. The implementation may be different on different boards. This binary can help developers to check the behavior of ALSA API.  BUG=chromium:601346 TEST=On samus, run `alsa_api_test --device hw:1,0 --drop`, will fail. TEST=On samus, run `alsa_api_test --device hw:1,0 --move`, will pass.  Change-Id: Id808d4fe69eabed52a5c42c4a6d8e1098965c5cb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340896 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="340896" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/audiotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/audiotest" ref="refs/changes/96/340896/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iea92341f0fe3d1094ea4311198b768bbaaf7cdbf" commit="4d99f2f3aaa923da70a8133555f14ab39c7d4001" commit_message="alsa_api_test: Add the option to test filling mmap buffer  Test the API to fill whole buffer with zeros. The sequence is: 1. Use snd_pcm_mmap_begin to get the mmap buffer. 2. Fill the mmap buffer with zeros using memset. 3. Do not call snd_pcm_mmap_commit. 4. Let device play for some periods. 5. Use snd_pcm_mmap_begin to get the mmap buffer. 6. Check mmap buffer contains all zeros.  BUG=chromium:601346 TEST=run `alsa_api_test --device hw:1,0 --fill` on samus.  Change-Id: Iea92341f0fe3d1094ea4311198b768bbaaf7cdbf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341842 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="341842" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/audiotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/audiotest" ref="refs/changes/42/341842/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2532778311e81efd79095fae2591241f4a0c7380" commit="2d6b7114b45dde609dd8ac8d2e8db7a839c1e1b1" commit_message="Revert &quot;autotest-chrome: exclude video tests on veyron platforms&quot;  This reverts commit 801b0340f44d7c38e6d97d42fedb6ff79f2994ea.  Veyron video HW acceleration is fixed.  BUG=chromium:608838 TEST=verified emerge works  Change-Id: I2532778311e81efd79095fae2591241f4a0c7380 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/343433 Commit-Ready: Kuang-che Wu &lt;kcwu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kuang-che Wu &lt;kcwu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="343433" owner_email="kcwu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/33/343433/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1a6e11293d75fb394f981d2d30b84b7f4a2f5bbb" commit="dd4e9821c450aff0356aa45516facc82960bb634" commit_message="testlog: populate should return self for convenience  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Locally  Change-Id: I1a6e11293d75fb394f981d2d30b84b7f4a2f5bbb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341893 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chun-ta Lin &lt;itspeter@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="341893" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/93/341893/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I428401e979b11292058a7398b0544e310496e268" commit="6a6d64214779eb09527c13beb710745864251b00" commit_message="[autotest] chameleon: Stabilize bluetooth connection sequence  Adjust these parameters to stabilize bluetooth connection. - Wait 20 seconds after disconnection to reset the state before connection. - Set connection retry time limit to 90 seconds because one trial may   take up to 15 seconds. - Wait 15 seconds after connection before checking bluetooth nodes.  BUG=chromium:607867 TEST=run audio_AudioBluetoothConnectionStability on peach_pi for 10 times. Change-Id: I428401e979b11292058a7398b0544e310496e268 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341253 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="341253" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/53/341253/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I377c0a22a5c707a6c18efc5fdc7de5bcd2be2c69" commit="f9d358c4aba35428d549fe2244956564e52b314f" commit_message="FROMLIST: pinctrl: rockchip: fix pull setting error for rk3399  This patch fixes the pinctrl pull bias setting, since the pull up/down setting is the contrary for gpio0(just the gpio0a and gpio0b) and gpio2(just the gpio2c and gpio2d).  From the TRM said, the gpio0a pull polarity setting: gpio0a_p GPIO0A PE/PS programmation section, every GPIO bit corresponding to 2bits[PS:PE] 2'b00: Z(Normal operation); 2'b11: weak 1(pull-up); 2'b01: weak 0(pull-down); 2'b10: Z(Normal operation);  Then, the other gpios setting as the following: gpio1a_p (e.g.: gpio1, gpio2a, gpio2b, gpio3...) GPIO1A PU/PD programmation section, every GPIO bit corresponding to 2bits 2'b00: Z(Normal operation); 2'b01: weak 1(pull-up); 2'b10: weak 0(pull-down); 2'b11: Z(Normal operation);  For example,(rk3399evb board) sdmmc_cd ---&gt;gpio0_a7 localhost / # io -r -4 0xff320040 ff320040: 00004d5f In general,the value should be 0x0000cd5f since the pin has been set in the dts.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53181 TEST=build and boot kevin rev1. TEST=Fixes the ec spi failed to respond. [60.753983] cros-ec-spi spi32765.0: EC failed to respond in time  Signed-off-by: David Wu &lt;david.wu@